se it even more. So you have to be careful with the direction you are measuring the current. It passes through the PI, and here is our current PI. And its output is basically just that. Besides that, I put here a feedforward action. What is it? My inverter PI output gives me a sinusoidal signal like this, which goes from -1 to +1. But a large part of the magnitude of this signal is the grid voltage. So if I am already compensating for this with the feedforward, I reduce the action of my PI. With this, I can have a slightly faster response because part of its action I have already reduced because I'm having an anticipatory action, which is the secret of feedforward. Here it will give an alternating number, a number in a format that would be like this. And the full PI, the rest, is just a feedforward action. So there is our control."

